{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"t":"Sample answers for Writing tasks","c":1,"h":0.018895348053517669,"w":0.3230452728271484,"x":0.096707816265669919,"y":0.069767442239004329},{"t":"TEST 7, WRITING TASK 1","w":0.36044995625813803,"c":1,"h":0.024068800945304503,"x":0.096556685152044963,"y":0.11751571209744449},{"x":0.098765434508680222,"t":"SAMPLE ANSWER","y":0.15400471129866178,"w":0.20576131184895832,"h":0.01750691675606264,"c":1},{"x":0.096592464389722743,"y":0.18769930221995168,"h":0.021433519109539501,"w":0.80477188110351561,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.5 score. Here is the","c":1},{"x":0.098412305530426347,"c":1,"y":0.20644539395196237,"w":0.20638814290364582,"t":"examiner's comment:","h":0.019789409300463801},{"x":0.14595837671752329,"t":"The candidate organises the information well and describes the trends in the","h":0.020493809550614417,"y":0.24055251028803615,"w":0.72248804728190108,"c":1},{"w":0.73491205851236985,"h":0.023810601206353699,"c":1,"y":0.25757494975761008,"x":0.14386755293453832,"t":"various groups, but the lack of data to support the descriptions is a significant"},{"y":0.27738877974403175,"x":0.1460039759930363,"w":0.7018412272135417,"c":1,"h":0.020020147936925525,"t":"omission. There is a clear progression throughout the response, with good"},{"c":1,"x":0.14795638035068465,"w":0.74520594278971353,"y":0.29369243125121558,"h":0.02216479298082763,"t":"management of cohesive devices [percentage of people who | during the same"},{"h":0.021531959866185613,"w":0.7780675252278646,"t":"period | in these segments of the chart | the groups in which | such facilities]. Lexis","x":0.14593013887887404,"y":0.31165228511973941,"c":1},{"t":"shows some flexibility and precision [on a weekly basis] and there is evidence of","x":0.14599491897792954,"y":0.32990927097984413,"c":1,"w":0.76152648925781241,"h":0.020400922346171302},{"y":0.34742323533596564,"t":"less common items [segments | major changes | most of the population | most\/","x":0.14390896018436308,"c":1,"w":0.75133295694986979,"h":0.021775316433855885},{"w":0.7822432454427084,"h":0.022986134595388008,"t":"least popular | with the exception of], with few errors in word choice [visualises | be","x":0.14590363535980144,"c":1,"y":0.36403199832121769},{"x":0.143941961283788,"y":0.38401021706996241,"w":0.78822901407877599,"c":1,"h":0.020407837327433676,"t":"| clients]. There is a variety of complex structures used with flexibility and accuracy,"},{"h":0.019547326545131138,"y":0.40182372549522483,"w":0.69151743570963542,"x":0.14600120894419916,"c":1,"t":"but there are also a few errors in grammatical control and in punctuation."},{"x":0.1007252831042942,"w":0.80470733642578118,"h":0.016856408652765165,"y":0.43770781602318065,"c":1,"t":"The chart visualises how often the US citizens be at fast-food restaurants in the"},{"y":0.45612671552031392,"t":"years 2003, 2006 and 2013.","x":0.10034905002266062,"h":0.02225194241329409,"c":1,"w":0.30937306722005209},{"w":0.81304066975911449,"h":0.021573193643343092,"c":1,"x":0.10481497620734188,"t":"From 2003 to 2006 the percenkage of people who have never eaten at a fast food","y":0.48055673047016756},{"x":0.10276647431796154,"h":0.020780516176257535,"c":1,"y":0.49945993964028768,"w":0.80476353963216152,"t":"restaurant has fallen by 1%, but on the other hand during the same period the number"},{"w":0.81712570190429701,"y":0.51616725951076292,"x":0.10274221478167524,"c":1,"t":"of clients who eat fast food everyday has also fallen to about 3% of the population.","h":0.02112932957805369},{"x":0.10484999030860478,"h":0.019629272892281335,"c":1,"y":0.53553518995156058,"t":"Since 2006, no other changes have occurred in these segments of the chart.","w":0.7368227132161459},{"x":0.1047823001505184,"t":"The major changes can be seen in the groups, who eak in a fast-food restaurant on a","w":0.81513748168945321,"h":0.023338230254372094,"c":1,"y":0.55917397231722143},{"c":1,"w":0.82937306722005222,"t":"weekly basis (once or several times a week) and in the groups in which people visit the","y":0.57863816555569314,"x":0.1048573408381146,"h":0.018913928414963754},{"y":0.59589090903175301,"h":0.017435766923273199,"x":0.10482632188031507,"t":"fast-food restaurants once or twice a month or once a few months. While in 2006","c":1,"w":0.80267608642578137},{"w":0.82524291992187493,"t":"most of the US citizens ate at such facilities at least once a week, in 2013 most","x":0.10281190673332048,"h":0.017042340322433902,"y":0.6144982838687606,"c":1},{"x":0.10476792041540033,"y":0.63002734682925809,"w":0.79458028157552096,"t":"of the population did so only once or twice a month. It's clear that the fast-food","h":0.023427648735271034,"c":1},{"x":0.10273665521436119,"t":"restaurants were most popular in 2006 and least popular in 2013. However the number","w":0.82951853434244793,"y":0.64903874078846613,"h":0.021221153025632766,"c":1},{"w":0.77387827555338551,"t":"of people who eat in such restaurants only a few times every year didn't change.","x":0.10277196651238057,"y":0.66674574829115785,"c":1,"h":0.022401899555687166},{"w":0.78621887207031249,"h":0.020607123807406147,"y":0.69254762618249577,"t":"As a whole, with the exception of people who rarely or never eat fast food and in","x":0.10689848259396362,"c":1},{"w":0.79218109130859371,"c":1,"t":"addition, the small part of the population who eat every day, the peak of going to","x":0.10493826114141787,"h":0.017472676590558844,"y":0.71220930215936384},{"y":0.72865665253970202,"c":1,"w":0.83350240071614579,"x":0.10690027805637044,"t":"fast-food restaurants was reached in 2006 in contrast with 2013 when most of the","h":0.017079327496819507},{"y":0.74809659759358893,"h":0.017938599288814583,"t":"population spent time in them only once or twice a month.","w":0.55989425659179681,"c":1,"x":0.10686903142452707},{"x":0.10905349853987981,"y":0.94622093007652963,"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.037037035624186199,"t":"128","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.39483721299237268,"h":0.016454192297478354,"y":0.96768258536995222,"w":0.20824633280436194,"t":"leltsresources.org"}]}